hunger to work every day, to go

00:30:08.073 --> 00:30:11.443
to the studio every day, to say
yes to opportunities because the

00:30:11.443 --> 00:30:14.012
second you start
saying, "Oh no, I'm good."

00:30:14.012 --> 00:30:16.081
- "We made it."
- Exactly.

00:30:16.081 --> 00:30:18.216
- Or "I'm too good."
- Yeah.

00:30:18.216 --> 00:30:20.652
- What do you think?
- For them?

00:30:20.652 --> 00:30:21.853
- Or about the game?

00:30:21.853 --> 00:30:25.323
Where do you think, while
I've got you for another second,

00:30:25.323 --> 00:30:28.292
where is the current state
of EDM in your guy's opinion?

00:30:28.292 --> 00:30:31.017
Obviously it was a that space,
I don't know, eight years ago,

00:30:31.017 --> 00:30:33.862
nine years ago most people
didn't know about. I still think

00:30:33.862 --> 00:30:35.450
there's a lot of people who
are watching who are 40,

00:30:35.450 --> 00:30:38.224
50-year-old marketing dudes that
have no idea what this space is

00:30:38.224 --> 00:30:40.629
and they're going to Google it. 
But obviously when you start

00:30:40.629 --> 00:30:44.152
